      },
      {
        "narration": "Inside rested everyday items of the era: a fountain pen, a pack of cigarettes, and a alphabet block set.",
        "visual_query": "vintage 1930s consumer artifacts",
        "visual_fallback": "old museum objects"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Engineers buried the torpedo-shaped vault fifty feet underground at the Flushing Meadows site for the 1939 World's Fair.",
